course: dictionary
lesson: 763
title: Beady eyes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in the reader's mind. Beady is one of them. «Look closely at a chicken's scaly feet, sharp claws and beady eye as it stalks across the yard, and you are looking at a living dinosaur.»
explain: Beady means small, round and shiny, like a bead. A bead is a tiny ball of glass or plastic, so beady eyes are small, round and bright. Look at the words around it: the chicken is stalking across the yard, so its beady eye tells you it is alert and watching.
explain: Beady has a second meaning that people use informally: watching very closely and suspiciously. Context shows you which meaning is used. Ask yourself what the creature or person is doing, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Beady is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in beady eyes. Its forms are beady, beadier and beadiest.
fact: «Beady» means small, round and shiny, like a bead, and it is mostly used about eyes.
fact: Informally, «beady» can mean watching very closely and suspiciously, as in «a beady eye».
fact: The phrase «keep a beady eye on» means watch carefully, often a teacher or parent.
fact: In stories, birds, rats and villains often have beady eyes, which makes them seem sharp, alert and a bit sneaky.
exercise: «Look closely at a chicken's scaly feet, sharp claws and beady eye as it stalks across the yard.» What does beady mean in this sentence? | Big and soft | Sleepy and slow | *Small, round and shiny, with a sharp, watchful look | Coloured like a rainbow
exercise: Mum says, «I'll keep a beady eye on you while you cook.» What does keep a beady eye on mean? | Close your eyes to | Buy a present for | *Watch carefully | Forget about
exercise: Which of these describes beady eyes, the small round shiny kind? | Soft and warm | *Small, round and shiny | Long and wobbly | Huge and hairy
test: «The rat's beady eyes shone in the dark.» What does beady describe here? | Loud and noisy | Very long and thin | Soft and fluffy | *Small, round and shiny
test: Which sentence uses beady in the informal sense of watching closely? | *The teacher kept a beady eye on the back row. | The rat had two beady eyes. | The beads on the necklace were beady. | The hen's beady eye was closed.
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to beady, in the sense of watching closely? | Cheerful | Careless | Sleepy | *Watchful
